<urn:aspace:01-projects-picard-05-marina-cleaning-bos-sop-b3-warp-core-execution-06-finance-wonderwoman-thunderbolts-jtbd-002-marina-transverse-finance-money-gate-md> a aspace:Document ;
    rdfs:label "JTBD-002 MARINA Transverse Finance Money Gate  ## Job When 05 Marina Cleaning BOS & SOP prepares any B2 or B3 action across the eight domains, Finance must verify price, margin, budget, cost, payment, refund, tax/legal dependency, approval, and leakage boundary before execution or launch.  ## Trigger Use this gate before: - publishing a price, quote, offer, package, membership, or service promise; - spending money, buying tools, assigning labor, or launching paid channels; - billing, refunding, collecting payments, or changing payment terms; - launching field/client/member/entity work with cost or liability exposure; - running work where margin, cash, or tax/entity implications are unclear.  ## Output A dated Finance readiness decision: - FINANCE_READY - NEEDS_MODEL - BLOCKED_LEAKAGE  ## Readiness Checks | Check | Question | | --- | --- | | Price | What is charged or budgeted? | | Cost | What labor, tools, supplies, compliance, or delivery costs exist? | | Margin | Is the work profitable or intentionally subsidized? | | Cash | When is money received or paid? | | Refund/exception | What happens when delivery changes or fails? | | Approval | Who can approve spend, price, or payment terms? | | Tax/legal | Does Legal/J03 need review? | | Leakage | What unpriced labor or hidden cost can break the model? |  ## Guardrail No field job may launch without quote, labor/supply cost, route cost, payment terms, margin, and refund/exception boundary.  ## Proof Attach the Finance packet, price/margin model, approval proof, cross-domain dependencies, and final Finance decision." ;
    aspace:seau <urn:aspace:01-projects-picard> ;
    dct:modified "2026-06-02" ;
    aspace:mots 193 .

